component sim_toolsetter "Simulated tool setter for the LCNC Suite sim configs: the probe input trips where a real tool setter would";

description
"""
The sim configs have no probe hardware: the WebUI's "Simulate probe trip"
pulses the \\fBprobe-in\\fR signal by hand. For the tool setter this
component trips the probe itself, in the servo thread, when the tool TIP
reaches the plate: the control point (joints 0..2, the slide positions) is
inside the plate's X/Y window and its Z minus the spindle tool's TABLE
length is at or below the plate surface. The table length is the sim's
physical length of the tool, so a measurement returns it (to a servo
period of the probe feed) and nothing drifts from run to run.

The plate is PHYSICAL: a fixed constant per sim profile (setp in its
core_sim_N.hal), not the WebUI's setting — the WebUI's tool setter must name
the same point, or it measures wrong by the difference, like a machine with
a mis-set reference. The control point is the JOINT position
(joint.N.pos-fb), never the motor position with its home offset. The table
length is set by sim_toolsetter_feed.py. No length (a tool without a table
length, an empty spindle) = no automatic trip: the probe finds nothing, as
on a machine without a tool setter. The manual trip stays: \\fBout\\fR =
contact OR \\fBmanual\\fR.

The tool is taken as VERTICAL (the 3-axis and XYZAC sims; the TWP sim's
head must stand at B0/C0 for a measurement).
""";

pin in float x "control point X, machine units (joint.0.pos-fb)";
pin in float y "control point Y (joint.1.pos-fb)";
pin in float z "control point Z (joint.2.pos-fb)";
pin in float plate_x "tool setter centre X, G53 — fixed per profile (setp)";
pin in float plate_y "tool setter centre Y, G53 — fixed per profile (setp)";
pin in float plate_z "plate surface Z, G53 — fixed per profile (setp)";
pin in float radius = 10.0 "half size of the X/Y trip window";
pin in float tool_length "the spindle tool's TABLE length (Z offset) — the sim's physical length";
pin in bit enable "a positive tool length is known (sim_toolsetter_feed.py)";
pin in bit manual "the WebUI's manual trip (probe-in)";
pin out bit contact "the tool tip touches the simulated plate";
pin out bit out "to motion.probe-input: contact OR manual";

function _ fp;
license "GPL";
author "LCNC Suite";
;;

#include "rtapi_math.h"

FUNCTION(_) {
    contact = enable && tool_length > 0.0
        && fabs(x - plate_x) <= radius
        && fabs(y - plate_y) <= radius
        && (z - tool_length) <= plate_z;
    out = contact || manual;
}
